  "goodToKnow": "Die Homöopathie is homeopathy. It was founded around 1796 by the German doctor Samuel Hahnemann, and it's still popular in Germany: many people take Globuli (tiny sugar pills), and some insurers have paid for it. Scientific studies show no effect beyond placebo, and the debate is heated; in 2024 the health minister proposed ending statutory insurance coverage. Homöopathisch means homeopathic, also used ironically for tiny amounts: eine homöopathische Dosis."
